{"sha":"d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff","node_id":"C_kwDOVSxolNoAKGQ3MTY5ODI2NDg3OGY4ZGFjY2VjNzAzYjFkMWY2ZDIwNWFhZDQ3ZmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ren","email":"ren@agentworld.me","date":"2026-10-30T02:24:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"Ren","email":"ren@agentworld.me","date":"2026-10-30T02:24:20Z"},"message":"Recheck feed v2, baseline pins/imports, field-level diffs, change webhooks, unified timeline\n\nAicom improvements 1-5 (alexar76/aicom#13), all additive:\n- Feed v2: every history record gains seq, record_id, schema_version\n  and a hash chain (prev_hash/record_hash over canonical content);\n  legacy rows backfilled deterministically at store open. Default\n  GET /v1/recheck/feed body is byte-identical; ?v=2 / ?since_seq= /\n  ?watch_id= / ?url= serve envelopes, cursor mode ascending with\n  X-Recheck-Feed-* headers exposing the chain head.\n- GET /v1/recheck/history[/<record_id>]: envelope reads + stateless\n  compare_seq baseline comparison.\n- Baseline pins (a pinned snapshot governs the watch's diff) and\n  imports (validated by recomputing the schema hash from the\n  supplied schema; provenance stored) behind the fleet-internal\n  secret, mirroring /v1/internal/claims-history. No public writes.\n- field_changes[] beside legacy changes[] in every Recheck result,\n  derived from the stored fingerprint components.\n- Per-watch change webhooks (internal-secret config): CHANGED only,\n  HMAC-SHA256 signed over the raw body, SSRF-checked at config and\n  send time, bounded retries, every attempt recorded, dead_letter\n  readable via the authenticated deliveries read.\n- GET /v1/resource/timeline: Recheck events + RouteVerdict\n  /v1/history + latest CDP catalogue snapshot state for one URL,\n  sources named, failures degrade to 'unavailable'.\nTests: 467 -> 484 passed.","tree":{"sha":"e600da74be2055d3dacf94d1ab7171f406f3fcbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuincyGB/stall-row/git/trees/e600da74be2055d3dacf94d1ab7171f406f3fcbb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuincyGB/stall-row/git/commits/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuincyGB/stall-row/commits/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff","html_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB/stall-row/commit/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuincyGB/stall-row/commits/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff/comments","author":null,"committer":null,"parents":[{"sha":"9303c9d6e9862c599711e979a8acba342dc634d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuincyGB/stall-row/commits/9303c9d6e9862c599711e979a8acba342dc634d7","html_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB/stall-row/commit/9303c9d6e9862c599711e979a8acba342dc634d7"}],"stats":{"total":1925,"additions":1910,"deletions":15},"files":[{"sha":"dd11f941819b731903881481b5fbc41b96d55c78","filename":"README.md","status":"modified","additions":13,"deletions":1,"changes":14,"blob_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB/stall-row/blob/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff/README.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB/stall-row/raw/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff/README.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuincyGB/stall-row/contents/README.md?ref=d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff","patch":"@@ -55,7 +55,19 @@ Recheck responses as JSONL (one object per line, newest first, last\n 100), a public observatory feed: every completed check's exact\n response object, recorded in the store at check time. Checks from\n before the history existed are seeded from the stored watch state\n-and carry only the fields that state persisted. Pack semantics: minting is idempotent on\n+and carry only the fields that state persisted. Feed v2 (additive):\n+every history record also carries a sequence number, a record_id,\n+and a hash chain over its canonical content — `GET /v1/recheck/feed?v=2&since_seq=N`\n+serves envelopes in gap-proof cursor mode (filters: `watch_id`,\n+`url`); `GET /v1/recheck/history[/<record_id>]` reads the same\n+records as JSON; `GET /v1/resource/timeline?url=` merges Recheck\n+events, RouteVerdict's check history, and the latest CDP catalogue\n+snapshot state for one resource, each source named. Recheck results\n+carry a structured `field_changes` array beside the legacy\n+`changes[]`. Baseline pins/imports and per-watch CHANGED webhooks\n+(HMAC-signed, bounded retries, dead-lettered readably) exist behind\n+the fleet-internal secret at `/v1/internal/recheck/*` — there is no\n+public mutation endpoint. Pack semantics: minting is idempotent on\n the payment's EIP-3009 authorization nonce, so a re-presented payment\n returns the pack it already bought; a credit is reserved atomically\n before each check and refunded when the check itself fails (our"},{"sha":"8406b54cb85cb36cae5db3100db756d5d3b1989d","filename":"app/discovery.py","status":"modified","additions":7,"deletions":1,"changes":8,"blob_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB/stall-row/blob/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff/app%2Fdiscovery.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB/stall-row/raw/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff/app%2Fdiscovery.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuincyGB/stall-row/contents/app%2Fdiscovery.py?ref=d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff","patch":"@@ -1707,6 +1707,10 @@ def skill_md(settings: Settings, base_url: str) -> str:\n         f\"- `GET {base_url}/.well-known/x402` — machine-readable manifest\",\n         f\"- `POST {base_url}/v1/recheck/pack-balance` — a pack's credits + expiry (pack id required)\",\n         f\"- `GET {base_url}/v1/recheck/feed` — recent Recheck results as JSONL, newest first (public observatory feed)\",\n+        f\"- `GET {base_url}/v1/recheck/feed?v=2&since_seq=N` — feed v2: each line an envelope (seq, record_id, schema_version, prev_hash, record_hash, record); since_seq is the gap-proof cursor mode (ascending), watch_id / url filter\",\n+        f\"- `GET {base_url}/v1/recheck/history` — recorded check history as envelopes, oldest first (?watch_id=, ?url=, ?compare_seq= for a stateless baseline comparison); `GET {base_url}/v1/recheck/history/<record_id>` — one snapshot\",\n+        f\"- `GET {base_url}/v1/resource/timeline?url=` — unified per-resource timeline: Recheck events + RouteVerdict check history + CDP catalogue snapshot state, each source named\",\n+        \"- Recheck results carry a structured `field_changes` array (path, op, before, after, severity, category) beside the legacy `changes[]`. Watch baselines can be pinned/imported and CHANGED results pushed to a signed per-watch webhook — both mutations are fleet-internal-secret gated (`/v1/internal/recheck/*`), never public writes\",\n     ]\n     return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n \n@@ -1735,6 +1739,8 @@ def llms_txt(settings: Settings, base_url: str) -> str:\n         f\"- GET {base_url}/health — free liveness check\",\n         f\"- GET {base_url}/.well-known/x402 — manifest\",\n         f\"- POST {base_url}/v1/recheck/pack-balance — free pack balance (pack id required)\",\n-        f\"- GET {base_url}/v1/recheck/feed — free Recheck results feed (JSONL, newest first)\",\n+        f\"- GET {base_url}/v1/recheck/feed — free Recheck results feed (JSONL, newest first); ?v=2&since_seq=N for the hash-chained cursor mode\",\n+        f\"- GET {base_url}/v1/recheck/history — free recorded history (envelopes); /v1/recheck/history/<record_id> for one snapshot\",\n+        f\"- GET {base_url}/v1/resource/timeline?url= — free unified per-resource timeline (Recheck + RouteVerdict + catalogue snapshot)\",\n     ]\n     return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\""},{"sha":"47bbad21da549db8df03e1cae5bd858a39c9414e","filename":"app/main.py","status":"modified","additions":333,"deletions":5,"changes":338,"blob_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB/stall-row/blob/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff/app%2Fmain.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB/stall-row/raw/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff/app%2Fmain.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuincyGB/stall-row/contents/app%2Fmain.py?ref=d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff","patch":"@@ -22,6 +22,14 @@\n         POST /v1/internal/nudges (owner read, fleet-internal secret)\n         POST /v1/internal/claims-history (claims history snapshot\n              upload, fleet-internal secret)\n+        GET  /v1/recheck/history[/<record_id>] (recorded checks as\n+             feed-v2 envelopes — seq, record_id, hash chain)\n+        GET  /v1/resource/timeline?url= (unified per-resource\n+             timeline: Recheck events + RouteVerdict history +\n+             catalogue snapshot state — see services/timeline.py)\n+        POST /v1/internal/recheck/baseline/{pin,unpin,import} and\n+             /v1/internal/recheck/webhooks[/deliveries] (watch\n+             mutations, fleet-internal secret — see services/recheck.py)\n \n Recheck packs: POST /v1/recheck presenting a pack id (body field\n `pack_id` or X-Recheck-Pack header) spends a prepaid credit instead\n@@ -93,6 +101,7 @@\n from .services import reads as reads_svc\n from .services import recheck as recheck_svc\n from .services import rotalerts as rotalerts_svc\n+from .services import timeline as timeline_svc\n from .services import watch as watch_svc\n from .services import scout as scout_svc\n from .services import seller as seller_svc\n@@ -1120,7 +1129,7 @@ async def recheck_pack_balance(req: RecheckPackBalanceRequest):\n \n \n @app.get(\"/v1/recheck/feed\")\n-async def recheck_feed():\n+async def recheck_feed(request: Request):\n     \"\"\"Free public feed of recent Recheck results: one JSON object\n     per line (JSONL), newest first, bounded to the last\n     recheck_svc.FEED_LIMIT recorded checks. This is the observatory\n@@ -1131,10 +1140,157 @@ async def recheck_feed():\n     before the history existed are seeded from the stored watch\n     state and carry only the fields that state persisted (no\n     status/changes/summary — see services/recheck.py). Empty\n-    history returns an empty body with 200.\"\"\"\n-    records = _recheck_store.recent_checks()\n-    body = \"\".join(json.dumps(r, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\" for r in records)\n-    return PlainTextResponse(body, media_type=\"application/x-ndjson\")\n+    history returns an empty body with 200.\n+\n+    Feed v2 (additive, backwards compatible): with NO parameters\n+    the body above is byte-identical to the original feed. Every\n+    history record also carries a monotonically increasing seq, a\n+    record_id, a schema_version, and a hash chain (prev_hash /\n+    record_hash). Pass ?v=2 — or any of ?watch_id=, ?url=,\n+    ?since_seq= — and each line is the envelope {seq, record_id,\n+    schema_version, prev_hash, record_hash, record}. since_seq=N\n+    is the cursor mode: records with seq > N, ascending, bounded by\n+    ?limit= (default FEED_LIMIT, max 1000); seq continuity across\n+    pages proves nothing was silently dropped. X-Recheck-Feed-\n+    Latest-Seq and X-Recheck-Feed-Count headers ride on every\n+    response so a poller can see the chain head either way.\"\"\"\n+    params = request.query_params\n+    v2 = (\n+        params.get(\"v\") == \"2\"\n+        or \"watch_id\" in params\n+        or \"url\" in params\n+        or \"since_seq\" in params\n+    )\n+    headers = {\n+        \"X-Recheck-Feed-Latest-Seq\": str(_recheck_store.latest_seq()),\n+        \"X-Recheck-Feed-Count\": str(_recheck_store.check_history_count()),\n+    }\n+    if not v2:\n+        records = _recheck_store.recent_checks()\n+        body = \"\".join(json.dumps(r, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\" for r in records)\n+        return PlainTextResponse(\n+            body, media_type=\"application/x-ndjson\", headers=headers\n+        )\n+    try:\n+        since_seq = (\n+            int(params[\"since_seq\"]) if \"since_seq\" in params else None\n+        )\n+        limit = int(params.get(\"limit\", recheck_svc.FEED_LIMIT))\n+    except ValueError:\n+        return JSONResponse(\n+            {\"error\": \"since_seq and limit must be integers\"},\n+            status_code=422,\n+        )\n+    envelopes = _recheck_store.feed_rows(\n+        watch_id=params.get(\"watch_id\"),\n+        url=params.get(\"url\"),\n+        since_seq=since_seq,\n+        limit=limit,\n+        ascending=since_seq is not None,\n+    )\n+    if envelopes:\n+        headers[\"X-Recheck-Feed-First-Seq\"] = str(envelopes[0][\"seq\"])\n+        headers[\"X-Recheck-Feed-Last-Seq\"] = str(envelopes[-1][\"seq\"])\n+    body = \"\".join(json.dumps(e, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\" for e in envelopes)\n+    return PlainTextResponse(\n+        body, media_type=\"application/x-ndjson\", headers=headers\n+    )\n+\n+\n+@app.get(\"/v1/recheck/history\")\n+async def recheck_history(request: Request):\n+    \"\"\"Free read of the recorded check history as feed-v2 envelopes\n+    (oldest first): ?watch_id= and/or ?url= filter, ?limit= bounds\n+    (default 100, max 1000). ?compare_seq=N adds a stateless\n+    baseline comparison: the newest record in the filtered history\n+    diffed against the record with seq N (which must be in the same\n+    filtered history) — {changes, field_changes} computed on the\n+    fly from the two stored fingerprints, nothing mutated.\"\"\"\n+    params = request.query_params\n+    try:\n+        limit = int(params.get(\"limit\", 100))\n+        compare_seq = (\n+            int(params[\"compare_seq\"]) if \"compare_seq\" in params else None\n+        )\n+    except ValueError:\n+        return JSONResponse(\n+            {\"error\": \"limit and compare_seq must be integers\"},\n+            status_code=422,\n+        )\n+    envelopes = _recheck_store.feed_rows(\n+        watch_id=params.get(\"watch_id\"),\n+        url=params.get(\"url\"),\n+        limit=limit,\n+        ascending=True,\n+    )\n+    out: dict = {\n+        \"count\": len(envelopes),\n+        \"latest_seq\": _recheck_store.latest_seq(),\n+        \"records\": envelopes,\n+    }\n+    pin_key = None\n+    if params.get(\"watch_id\") and params.get(\"url\"):\n+        pin_key = f\"{params['watch_id']}\\n{params['url']}\"\n+    if pin_key:\n+        out[\"baseline_pin\"] = _recheck_store.get_pin(pin_key)\n+    if compare_seq is not None:\n+        base = next(\n+            (e for e in envelopes if e[\"seq\"] == compare_seq), None\n+        )\n+        if base is None:\n+            return JSONResponse(\n+                {\n+                    \"error\": \"compare_seq is not in the filtered history\",\n+                },\n+                status_code=404,\n+            )\n+        newest = envelopes[-1] if envelopes else None\n+        if newest is None or newest[\"seq\"] == compare_seq:\n+            out[\"comparison\"] = {\n+                \"against_seq\": compare_seq,\n+                \"changes\": [],\n+                \"field_changes\": [],\n+            }\n+        else:\n+            before = base[\"record\"].get(\"current\") or {}\n+            after = newest[\"record\"].get(\"current\") or {}\n+            out[\"comparison\"] = {\n+                \"against_seq\": compare_seq,\n+                \"against_checked_at\": base[\"record\"].get(\"checked_at\"),\n+                \"changes\": recheck_svc._diff(before, after),\n+                \"field_changes\": recheck_svc.fingerprint_field_changes(\n+                    before, after\n+                ),\n+            }\n+    return out\n+\n+\n+@app.get(\"/v1/recheck/history/{record_id}\")\n+async def recheck_history_record(record_id: str):\n+    \"\"\"One recorded check by record_id (or by seq, as ?seq=N on the\n+    collection read) — the individual snapshot read behind the\n+    history list.\"\"\"\n+    envelope = _recheck_store.record_by_id(record_id)\n+    if envelope is None:\n+        return JSONResponse({\"error\": \"unknown record_id\"}, status_code=404)\n+    return envelope\n+\n+\n+@app.get(\"/v1/resource/timeline\")\n+async def resource_timeline(url: str):\n+    \"\"\"Free unified per-resource timeline: Recheck events from this\n+    service's history, RouteVerdict check events from that\n+    service's free /v1/history read, and the resource's state in\n+    the latest CDP catalogue snapshot held here — merged by time,\n+    each section naming its source and whether it contributed (see\n+    services/timeline.py). A source that cannot answer is reported\n+    unavailable, never filled in.\"\"\"\n+    url = url.strip()\n+    if not url:\n+        return JSONResponse({\"error\": \"url is required\"}, status_code=422)\n+    return await timeline_svc.build_timeline(\n+        _fetch_client(), _recheck_store, _index_store, url\n+    )\n \n \n # --- Fleet Pass ---------------------------------------------------------------\n@@ -2129,6 +2285,178 @@ async def internal_claims_history(request: Request):\n     }\n \n \n+# --- Recheck watch mutations (baseline pins/imports, change webhooks) ------------\n+# Mutations on a watch's state, gated by the fleet-internal secret\n+# exactly like /v1/internal/claims-history: secret unset = 404,\n+# wrong secret = 403. Why not claim sessions: those bind to a\n+# CLAIMED ORIGIN; a Recheck watch (watch_id + URL) has no owner\n+# session in the existing model, so the internal secret is the only\n+# existing credential that can authorize watch-level mutation\n+# without inventing a new auth system. Reads stay public (the feed\n+# already publishes the same records); only writes are gated.\n+\n+def _internal_gate(request: Request) -> JSONResponse | None:\n+    secret = os.environ.get(\"FLEET_INTERNAL_SECRET\", \"\")\n+    if not secret:\n+        return JSONResponse({\"detail\": \"Not Found\"}, status_code=404)\n+    provided = request.headers.get(\"x-fleet-internal-secret\", \"\")\n+    if not hmac.compare_digest(provided, secret):\n+        return JSONResponse(\n+            {\"detail\": \"fleet internal secret required\"}, status_code=403\n+        )\n+    return None\n+\n+\n+def _watch_key_of(watch_id: str | None, url: str) -> str:\n+    wid = (watch_id or \"\").strip() or recheck_svc.default_watch_id(url.strip())\n+    return f\"{wid}\\n{url.strip()}\"\n+\n+\n+class BaselinePinRequest(BaseModel):\n+    watch_id: str | None = Field(default=None, description=\"Watch id; defaults to the URL's implicit watch\")\n+    url: str = Field(description=\"The watch's target URL\")\n+    seq: int = Field(description=\"History seq of the snapshot to pin as the baseline\")\n+\n+\n+class BaselineUnpinRequest(BaseModel):\n+    watch_id: str | None = None\n+    url: str\n+\n+\n+class BaselineImportRequest(BaseModel):\n+    watch_id: str | None = None\n+    url: str\n+    kind: str = Field(description=\"'x402' or 'web'\")\n+    current: dict = Field(description=\"The snapshot's fingerprint, in the shape Recheck stores\")\n+    checked_at: str = Field(description=\"ISO timestamp the snapshot claims\")\n+    source: str = Field(description=\"Where this snapshot came from (provenance, stored verbatim)\")\n+    schema_: dict | None = Field(\n+        default=None,\n+        alias=\"schema\",\n+        description=\"For x402 snapshots claiming a schema_hash: the raw output schema; it must hash to the claimed schema_hash or the import is refused\",\n+    )\n+\n+\n+class ChangeWebhookRequest(BaseModel):\n+    watch_id: str | None = None\n+    url: str\n+    webhook_url: str = Field(description=\"Public https URL; SSRF-checked before storing\")\n+    secret: str = Field(description=\"HMAC-SHA256 key for X-Recheck-Signature\")\n+    enabled: bool = True\n+\n+\n+@app.post(\"/v1/internal/recheck/baseline/pin\")\n+async def internal_baseline_pin(req: BaselinePinRequest, request: Request):\n+    \"\"\"Pin one recorded history snapshot as the watch's baseline:\n+    while pinned, recheck() diffs against the pinned fingerprint\n+    instead of the latest state. The pin must name a record that\n+    belongs to this watch.\"\"\"\n+    if (gate := _internal_gate(request)) is not None:\n+        return gate\n+    key = _watch_key_of(req.watch_id, req.url)\n+    envelope = _recheck_store.pin_baseline(key, req.seq, source=\"internal-pin\")\n+    if envelope is None:\n+        return JSONResponse(\n+            {\"error\": \"no history record with that seq for this watch\"},\n+            status_code=404,\n+        )\n+    return {\"ok\": True, \"watch_key\": key, \"pin\": _recheck_store.get_pin(key)}\n+\n+\n+@app.post(\"/v1/internal/recheck/baseline/unpin\")\n+async def internal_baseline_unpin(req: BaselineUnpinRequest, request: Request):\n+    if (gate := _internal_gate(request)) is not None:\n+        return gate\n+    key = _watch_key_of(req.watch_id, req.url)\n+    removed = _recheck_store.unpin_baseline(key)\n+    return {\"ok\": True, \"watch_key\": key, \"was_pinned\": removed}\n+\n+\n+@app.post(\"/v1/internal/recheck/baseline/import\")\n+async def internal_baseline_import(req: BaselineImportRequest, request: Request):\n+    \"\"\"Import an external snapshot as a watch's baseline. The\n+    snapshot is validated by recomputation BEFORE anything is\n+    stored (services/recheck.py validate_imported_snapshot): an\n+    x402 snapshot claiming a schema_hash must carry the raw schema\n+    and the schema must hash to the claim — a forged import is a\n+    loud 422 and stores nothing. What lands carries its provenance\n+    (imported=true, source, imported_at).\"\"\"\n+    if (gate := _internal_gate(request)) is not None:\n+        return gate\n+    try:\n+        recheck_svc.validate_imported_snapshot(\n+            req.kind, req.current, req.schema_\n+        )\n+    except ValueError as e:\n+        return JSONResponse({\"error\": str(e)}, status_code=422)\n+    key = _watch_key_of(req.watch_id, req.url)\n+    envelope = _recheck_store.import_baseline(\n+        key, req.kind, req.current, req.checked_at, req.source.strip() or \"unspecified\"\n+    )\n+    return {\"ok\": True, \"watch_key\": key, \"record\": envelope}\n+\n+\n+@app.post(\"/v1/internal/recheck/webhooks\")\n+async def internal_change_webhook(req: ChangeWebhookRequest, request: Request):\n+    \"\"\"Configure a watch's change webhook. The target must be a\n+    public https URL under the fleet's SSRF discipline — checked\n+    before storing and again at send time. On every CHANGED result\n+    for the watch, the recorded event is POSTed signed with\n+    HMAC-SHA256 (X-Recheck-Signature) over the raw body; deliveries\n+    retry bounded, record every attempt, and dead-letter readably.\n+    The secret is never echoed back.\"\"\"\n+    if (gate := _internal_gate(request)) is not None:\n+        return gate\n+    webhook_url = req.webhook_url.strip()\n+    if not webhook_url.startswith(\"https://\"):\n+        return JSONResponse(\n+            {\"error\": \"webhook_url must be an https URL\"}, status_code=422\n+        )\n+    try:\n+        await asyncio.to_thread(fetch_svc.ssrf_check, webhook_url)\n+    except ValueError as e:\n+        return JSONResponse(\n+            {\"error\": f\"webhook_url refused by the SSRF guard: {e}\"},\n+            status_code=422,\n+        )\n+    if not req.secret.strip():\n+        return JSONResponse(\n+            {\"error\": \"secret is required\"}, status_code=422\n+        )\n+    key = _watch_key_of(req.watch_id, req.url)\n+    _recheck_store.set_change_webhook(\n+        key, webhook_url, req.secret, req.enabled\n+    )\n+    return {\n+        \"ok\": True,\n+        \"watch_key\": key,\n+        \"webhook_url\": webhook_url,\n+        \"enabled\": req.enabled,\n+    }\n+\n+\n+@app.get(\"/v1/internal/recheck/webhooks/deliveries\")\n+async def internal_change_deliveries(request: Request):\n+    \"\"\"Authenticated read of change-webhook deliveries (status,\n+    attempts, last error, full payload) — where a dead_letter is\n+    found and diagnosed. Optional ?watch_id= + ?url= scope it to\n+    one watch.\"\"\"\n+    if (gate := _internal_gate(request)) is not None:\n+        return gate\n+    params = request.query_params\n+    key = None\n+    if params.get(\"url\"):\n+        key = _watch_key_of(params.get(\"watch_id\"), params[\"url\"])\n+    try:\n+        limit = int(params.get(\"limit\", 50))\n+    except ValueError:\n+        return JSONResponse(\n+            {\"error\": \"limit must be an integer\"}, status_code=422\n+        )\n+    deliveries = _recheck_store.list_change_deliveries(key, limit)\n+    return {\"count\": len(deliveries), \"deliveries\": deliveries}\n+\n+\n # --- Human payment rail (internal mint) -------------------------------------------\n # A buyer who cannot pay via x402 sends exactly $5.00 USDC on Base\n # directly to the payTo wallet; the payment-rail watcher"},{"sha":"a8fcc8058246594d22ca3f158666e62b8f697ef4","filename":"app/services/recheck.py","status":"modified","additions":855,"deletions":8,"changes":863,"blob_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB/stall-row/blob/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff/app%2Fservices%2Frecheck.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB/stall-row/raw/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff/app%2Fservices%2Frecheck.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuincyGB/stall-row/contents/app%2Fservices%2Frecheck.py?ref=d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff","patch":"@@ -40,13 +40,28 @@\n per-check status/changes/summary of those earlier checks were\n never stored, so seeded records omit them — the feed serves what\n the store holds, never a reconstruction.\n+\n+Feed v2 + baselines + webhooks (2026-10-29, aicom improvements\n+1–5): every history record also carries a seq, a record_id, and a\n+hash chain (see FEED_SCHEMA_VERSION); the default feed body is\n+unchanged, the envelope rides the v2 parameters. A baseline PIN\n+(one recorded snapshot, internal-secret gated at the HTTP layer)\n+governs a watch's diff while it exists; an imported baseline is\n+validated by recomputation before it is stored and carries its\n+provenance. Results carry a structured field_changes array beside\n+the legacy changes[]. A watch may register one change webhook\n+(internal-secret gated): CHANGED results — never BASELINE or\n+UNCHANGED — are delivered as HMAC-signed events with bounded\n+retries and a readable dead-letter. The unified per-resource\n+timeline lives in services/timeline.py.\n \"\"\"\n \n from __future__ import annotations\n \n import asyncio\n import base64\n import hashlib\n+import hmac\n import json\n import logging\n import os\n@@ -105,6 +120,28 @@ def _iso_of(epoch_seconds: float) -> str:\n # this many of the most recent recorded check responses.\n FEED_LIMIT = 100\n \n+# --- feed v2: sequence + hash chain -------------------------------------\n+# Every history record also carries a monotonically increasing seq,\n+# a record_id, a schema_version, and a hash chain (prev_hash /\n+# record_hash over the record's canonical JSON). A poller reading\n+# with ?since_seq= can advance a cursor and PROVE nothing was\n+# silently dropped: seqs are continuous and each record_hash\n+# commits to its content and its predecessor. The legacy default\n+# feed shape (bare response objects) is unchanged; the envelope is\n+# served when a v2 parameter is present (see main.py).\n+FEED_SCHEMA_VERSION = 1\n+_FEED_GENESIS = \"genesis\"\n+\n+\n+def _canonical_record_json(record: dict) -> str:\n+    return json.dumps(record, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n+\n+\n+def _chain_hash(prev_hash: str, record: dict) -> str:\n+    return hashlib.sha256(\n+        f\"{prev_hash}\\n{_canonical_record_json(record)}\".encode(\"utf-8\")\n+    ).hexdigest()\n+\n # --- fleet check packs -----------------------------------------------------------\n #\n # The standing form of Fleet Check (services/fleetcheck.py): one\n@@ -493,8 +530,90 @@ def __init__(self, path: str, persistent: bool | None = None):\n                 )\n                 \"\"\"\n             )\n+            # Feed v2 (seq + hash chain), baseline pins, and the\n+            # per-watch change webhooks. All additive: existing rows\n+            # are backfilled deterministically by _backfill_chain.\n+            self._conn.execute(\n+                \"\"\"\n+                CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS feed_meta (\n+                    key TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n+                    value TEXT NOT NULL\n+                )\n+                \"\"\"\n+            )\n+            self._conn.execute(\n+                \"\"\"\n+                CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS recheck_baseline_pins (\n+                    watch_key TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n+                    seq INTEGER NOT NULL,\n+                    record_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n+                    pinned_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n+                    source TEXT\n+                )\n+                \"\"\"\n+            )\n+            self._conn.execute(\n+                \"\"\"\n+                CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS recheck_webhooks (\n+                    watch_key TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n+                    webhook_url TEXT NOT NULL,\n+                    secret TEXT NOT NULL,\n+                    enabled INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,\n+                    created_epoch REAL NOT NULL,\n+                    updated_epoch REAL NOT NULL\n+                )\n+                \"\"\"\n+            )\n+            self._conn.execute(\n+                \"\"\"\n+                CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS recheck_webhook_deliveries (\n+                    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n+                    event_id TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n+                    watch_key TEXT NOT NULL,\n+                    seq INTEGER,\n+                    url TEXT,\n+                    status TEXT NOT NULL,\n+                    attempts INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n+                    last_http_status INTEGER,\n+                    last_error TEXT,\n+                    created_epoch REAL NOT NULL,\n+                    updated_epoch REAL NOT NULL,\n+                    payload_json TEXT NOT NULL\n+                )\n+                \"\"\"\n+            )\n+            self._conn.execute(\n+                \"\"\"\n+                CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS recheck_webhook_attempts (\n+                    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n+                    delivery_id INTEGER NOT NULL,\n+                    attempt_no INTEGER NOT NULL,\n+                    epoch REAL NOT NULL,\n+                    http_status INTEGER,\n+                    error TEXT\n+                )\n+                \"\"\"\n+            )\n+            cols = {\n+                row[1]\n+                for row in self._conn.execute(\n+                    \"PRAGMA table_info(recheck_history)\"\n+                )\n+            }\n+            for col, decl in (\n+                (\"seq\", \"INTEGER\"),\n+                (\"record_id\", \"TEXT\"),\n+                (\"schema_version\", \"INTEGER\"),\n+                (\"prev_hash\", \"TEXT\"),\n+                (\"record_hash\", \"TEXT\"),\n+            ):\n+                if col not in cols:\n+                    self._conn.execute(\n+                        f\"ALTER TABLE recheck_history ADD COLUMN {col} {decl}\"\n+                    )\n             self._conn.commit()\n         self._seed_history_from_watches()\n+        self._backfill_chain()\n \n     @property\n     def path(self) -> str:\n@@ -580,23 +699,131 @@ def _seed_history_from_watches(self) -> None:\n                 )\n             self._conn.commit()\n \n-    def record_check(self, response: dict) -> None:\n-        \"\"\"Append one COMPLETED check's response to the history.\n-        Called by recheck() itself, so per-call, pack-spent, and\n-        scheduled-watch checks are all recorded exactly once, with\n-        the exact object the caller was answered with.\"\"\"\n+    # --- feed v2: chain state --------------------------------------\n+    # feed_meta carries the chain head: next_seq + last record_hash.\n+    # Backfill and live appends share _chain_locked so the chain is\n+    # built exactly one way.\n+\n+    def _feed_meta(self, key: str) -> str | None:\n+        row = self._conn.execute(\n+            \"SELECT value FROM feed_meta WHERE key = ?\", (key,)\n+        ).fetchone()\n+        return row[0] if row else None\n+\n+    def _set_feed_meta(self, key: str, value: str) -> None:\n+        self._conn.execute(\n+            \"INSERT OR REPLACE INTO feed_meta (key, value) VALUES (?, ?)\",\n+            (key, value),\n+        )\n+\n+    def _backfill_chain(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"Assign seq/record_id/hashes to every history row that\n+        lacks them, oldest first. Deterministic: the hash input is\n+        the stored response JSON itself, so re-running (or running\n+        on a copy of the store) reproduces the identical chain, and\n+        a store whose rows are already chained is untouched.\"\"\"\n+        with self._lock:\n+            rows = self._conn.execute(\n+                \"SELECT id, response_json, seq, record_hash \"\n+                \"FROM recheck_history ORDER BY id ASC\"\n+            ).fetchall()\n+            next_seq = self._feed_meta(\"next_seq\")\n+            seq = int(next_seq) if next_seq is not None else None\n+            prev_hash = self._feed_meta(\"last_hash\") or _FEED_GENESIS\n+            if seq is None:\n+                chained = [r for r in rows if r[2] is not None]\n+                seq = (max(r[2] for r in chained) + 1) if chained else 1\n+                if chained:\n+                    head = max(chained, key=lambda r: r[2])\n+                    prev_hash = head[3] or _FEED_GENESIS\n+            for row_id, raw, row_seq, _rh in rows:\n+                if row_seq is not None:\n+                    continue\n+                try:\n+                    record = json.loads(raw)\n+                except ValueError:\n+                    continue\n+                record_hash = _chain_hash(prev_hash, record)\n+                record_id = f\"rec_{record_hash[:24]}\"\n+                self._conn.execute(\n+                    \"UPDATE recheck_history SET seq = ?, record_id = ?, \"\n+                    \"schema_version = ?, prev_hash = ?, record_hash = ? \"\n+                    \"WHERE id = ?\",\n+                    (\n+                        seq,\n+                        record_id,\n+                        FEED_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n+                        prev_hash,\n+                        record_hash,\n+                        row_id,\n+                    ),\n+                )\n+                prev_hash = record_hash\n+                seq += 1\n+            self._set_feed_meta(\"next_seq\", str(seq))\n+            self._set_feed_meta(\"last_hash\", prev_hash)\n+            self._conn.commit()\n+\n+    _HISTORY_COLS = (\n+        \"seq, record_id, schema_version, prev_hash, record_hash, response_json\"\n+    )\n+\n+    @classmethod\n+    def _row_envelope(cls, row) -> dict | None:\n+        try:\n+            record = json.loads(row[5])\n+        except ValueError:\n+            return None\n+        return {\n+            \"seq\": row[0],\n+            \"record_id\": row[1],\n+            \"schema_version\": row[2],\n+            \"prev_hash\": row[3],\n+            \"record_hash\": row[4],\n+            \"record\": record,\n+        }\n+\n+    def record_check(self, response: dict) -> dict:\n+        \"\"\"Append one COMPLETED check's response to the history and\n+        return its feed envelope ({seq, record_id, schema_version,\n+        prev_hash, record_hash, record}). Called by recheck()\n+        itself, so per-call, pack-spent, and scheduled-watch checks\n+        are all recorded exactly once, with the exact object the\n+        caller was answered with.\"\"\"\n         key = f\"{response['watch_id']}\\n{response['url']}\"\n         with self._lock:\n+            next_seq = self._feed_meta(\"next_seq\")\n+            seq = int(next_seq) if next_seq is not None else 1\n+            prev_hash = self._feed_meta(\"last_hash\") or _FEED_GENESIS\n+            record_hash = _chain_hash(prev_hash, response)\n+            record_id = f\"rec_{record_hash[:24]}\"\n             self._conn.execute(\n                 \"INSERT INTO recheck_history \"\n-                \"(watch_key, checked_at, response_json) VALUES (?, ?, ?)\",\n+                \"(watch_key, checked_at, response_json, seq, record_id, \"\n+                \"schema_version, prev_hash, record_hash) \"\n+                \"VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n                 (\n                     key,\n                     response[\"checked_at\"],\n                     json.dumps(response, sort_keys=True),\n+                    seq,\n+                    record_id,\n+                    FEED_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n+                    prev_hash,\n+                    record_hash,\n                 ),\n             )\n+            self._set_feed_meta(\"next_seq\", str(seq + 1))\n+            self._set_feed_meta(\"last_hash\", record_hash)\n             self._conn.commit()\n+        return {\n+            \"seq\": seq,\n+            \"record_id\": record_id,\n+            \"schema_version\": FEED_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n+            \"prev_hash\": prev_hash,\n+            \"record_hash\": record_hash,\n+            \"record\": response,\n+        }\n \n     def recent_checks(self, limit: int = FEED_LIMIT) -> list[dict]:\n         \"\"\"The feed window: the most recent recorded check\n@@ -622,6 +849,351 @@ def check_history_count(self) -> int:\n             ).fetchone()\n         return int(row[0]) if row else 0\n \n+    def latest_seq(self) -> int:\n+        with self._lock:\n+            row = self._conn.execute(\n+                \"SELECT MAX(seq) FROM recheck_history\"\n+            ).fetchone()\n+        return int(row[0]) if row and row[0] is not None else 0\n+\n+    @staticmethod\n+    def _like_escape(text: str) -> str:\n+        return (\n+            text.replace(\"\\\\\", \"\\\\\\\\\").replace(\"%\", \"\\\\%\").replace(\"_\", \"\\\\_\")\n+        )\n+\n+    def feed_rows(\n+        self,\n+        watch_id: str | None = None,\n+        url: str | None = None,\n+        since_seq: int | None = None,\n+        limit: int = FEED_LIMIT,\n+        ascending: bool = False,\n+    ) -> list[dict]:\n+        \"\"\"History envelopes, filtered. Cursor mode (since_seq set)\n+        is ascending by construction — the caller advances its\n+        cursor to the last seq seen; continuity of seq across pages\n+        is the no-silent-gap proof. Default order is newest first,\n+        like the legacy feed.\"\"\"\n+        clauses: list[str] = []\n+        params: list = []\n+        if watch_id is not None and url is not None:\n+            clauses.append(\"watch_key = ?\")\n+            params.append(f\"{watch_id}\\n{url}\")\n+        elif watch_id is not None:\n+            clauses.append(\"watch_key LIKE ? ESCAPE '\\\\'\")\n+            params.append(f\"{self._like_escape(watch_id)}\\n%\")\n+        elif url is not None:\n+            clauses.append(\"watch_key LIKE ? ESCAPE '\\\\'\")\n+            params.append(f\"%\\n{self._like_escape(url)}\")\n+        if since_seq is not None:\n+            clauses.append(\"seq > ?\")\n+            params.append(int(since_seq))\n+            ascending = True\n+        where = f\"WHERE {' AND '.join(clauses)}\" if clauses else \"\"\n+        order = \"ASC\" if ascending else \"DESC\"\n+        with self._lock:\n+            rows = self._conn.execute(\n+                f\"SELECT {self._HISTORY_COLS} FROM recheck_history \"\n+                f\"{where} ORDER BY seq {order} LIMIT ?\",\n+                (*params, max(1, min(int(limit), 1000))),\n+            ).fetchall()\n+        out = []\n+        for row in rows:\n+            env = self._row_envelope(row)\n+            if env is not None:\n+                out.append(env)\n+        return out\n+\n+    def record_by_seq(self, seq: int) -> dict | None:\n+        with self._lock:\n+            row = self._conn.execute(\n+                f\"SELECT {self._HISTORY_COLS} FROM recheck_history \"\n+                \"WHERE seq = ?\",\n+                (int(seq),),\n+            ).fetchone()\n+        return self._row_envelope(row) if row else None\n+\n+    def record_by_id(self, record_id: str) -> dict | None:\n+        with self._lock:\n+            row = self._conn.execute(\n+                f\"SELECT {self._HISTORY_COLS} FROM recheck_history \"\n+                \"WHERE record_id = ?\",\n+                (record_id,),\n+            ).fetchone()\n+        return self._row_envelope(row) if row else None\n+\n+    def verify_chain(self) -> bool:\n+        \"\"\"Recompute the whole chain from the stored records; True\n+        only when every seq is continuous from 1 and every hash\n+        links. The feed's integrity claim, checkable in-process.\"\"\"\n+        with self._lock:\n+            rows = self._conn.execute(\n+                f\"SELECT {self._HISTORY_COLS} FROM recheck_history \"\n+                \"ORDER BY seq ASC\"\n+            ).fetchall()\n+        prev_hash = _FEED_GENESIS\n+        for expected_seq, row in enumerate(rows, start=1):\n+            env = self._row_envelope(row)\n+            if env is None or env[\"seq\"] != expected_seq:\n+                return False\n+            if env[\"prev_hash\"] != prev_hash:\n+                return False\n+            if env[\"record_hash\"] != _chain_hash(prev_hash, env[\"record\"]):\n+                return False\n+            prev_hash = env[\"record_hash\"]\n+        return True\n+\n+    # --- baseline pins + imports ------------------------------------\n+    # A pin makes one recorded snapshot THE baseline a watch diffs\n+    # against (recheck() consults pins before the latest-state row).\n+    # Pins and imports are mutations: the HTTP layer gates them\n+    # behind the fleet-internal secret (see main.py); the store just\n+    # keeps the state honestly, provenance included.\n+\n+    def pin_baseline(self, watch_key: str, seq: int, source: str) -> dict | None:\n+        env = self.record_by_seq(seq)\n+        if env is None:\n+            return None\n+        with self._lock:\n+            row = self._conn.execute(\n+                \"SELECT watch_key FROM recheck_history WHERE seq = ?\",\n+                (int(seq),),\n+            ).fetchone()\n+            if row is None or row[0] != watch_key:\n+                return None\n+            self._conn.execute(\n+                \"INSERT OR REPLACE INTO recheck_baseline_pins \"\n+                \"(watch_key, seq, record_id, pinned_at, source) \"\n+                \"VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n+                (\n+                    watch_key,\n+                    int(seq),\n+                    env[\"record_id\"],\n+                    _now_iso(),\n+                    source,\n+                ),\n+            )\n+            self._conn.commit()\n+        return env\n+\n+    def get_pin(self, watch_key: str) -> dict | None:\n+        with self._lock:\n+            row = self._conn.execute(\n+                \"SELECT seq, record_id, pinned_at, source FROM \"\n+                \"recheck_baseline_pins WHERE watch_key = ?\",\n+                (watch_key,),\n+            ).fetchone()\n+        if row is None:\n+            return None\n+        return {\n+            \"seq\": row[0],\n+            \"record_id\": row[1],\n+            \"pinned_at\": row[2],\n+            \"source\": row[3],\n+        }\n+\n+    def unpin_baseline(self, watch_key: str) -> bool:\n+        with self._lock:\n+            cur = self._conn.execute(\n+                \"DELETE FROM recheck_baseline_pins WHERE watch_key = ?\",\n+                (watch_key,),\n+            )\n+            self._conn.commit()\n+        return cur.rowcount > 0\n+\n+    def pinned_baseline(self, watch_key: str) -> dict | None:\n+        \"\"\"The pinned record's stored state in the watches-table\n+        shape ({kind, fingerprint, checked_at}), or None.\"\"\"\n+        pin = self.get_pin(watch_key)\n+        if pin is None:\n+            return None\n+        env = self.record_by_seq(pin[\"seq\"])\n+        if env is None:\n+            return None\n+        record = env[\"record\"]\n+        fingerprint = record.get(\"current\")\n+        if not isinstance(fingerprint, dict):\n+            return None\n+        return {\n+            \"kind\": record.get(\"kind\"),\n+            \"fingerprint\": fingerprint,\n+            \"checked_at\": record.get(\"checked_at\"),\n+        }\n+\n+    def import_baseline(\n+        self,\n+        watch_key: str,\n+        kind: str,\n+        fingerprint: dict,\n+        checked_at: str,\n+        source: str,\n+    ) -> dict:\n+        \"\"\"Store an externally supplied snapshot as the watch's\n+        baseline: it lands in the history as a record carrying its\n+        provenance (imported=true, source, imported_at) AND becomes\n+        the watch's stored state, so the next check diffs against\n+        it. Validation (fingerprint recomputation) happens in\n+        validate_imported_snapshot BEFORE this is called.\"\"\"\n+        watch_id, _, url = watch_key.partition(\"\\n\")\n+        record = {\n+            \"watch_id\": watch_id,\n+            \"url\": url,\n+            \"kind\": kind,\n+            \"status\": \"BASELINE\",\n+            \"changes\": [],\n+            \"field_changes\": [],\n+            \"current\": fingerprint,\n+            \"checked_at\": checked_at,\n+            \"summary\": (\n+                f\"Baseline imported from {source}; the next check for \"\n+                \"this watch diffs against this snapshot.\"\n+            ),\n+            \"imported\": True,\n+            \"provenance\": {\"source\": source, \"imported_at\": _now_iso()},\n+        }\n+        envelope = self.record_check(record)\n+        self.save(watch_key, kind, fingerprint, checked_at)\n+        return envelope\n+\n+    # --- per-watch change webhooks -----------------------------------\n+    # Config is a mutation (fleet-internal secret at the HTTP\n+    # layer); delivery state is fully recorded — every attempt, and\n+    # a terminal dead_letter after the bounded retries.\n+\n+    def set_change_webhook(\n+        self,\n+        watch_key: str,\n+        webhook_url: str,\n+        secret: str,\n+        enabled: bool = True,\n+    ) -> dict:\n+        now = time.time()\n+        with self._lock:\n+            self._conn.execute(\n+                \"INSERT INTO recheck_webhooks (watch_key, webhook_url, \"\n+                \"secret, enabled, created_epoch, updated_epoch) \"\n+                \"VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?) ON CONFLICT(watch_key) DO \"\n+                \"UPDATE SET webhook_url = excluded.webhook_url, \"\n+                \"secret = excluded.secret, enabled = excluded.enabled, \"\n+                \"updated_epoch = excluded.updated_epoch\",\n+                (watch_key, webhook_url, secret, 1 if enabled else 0, now, now),\n+            )\n+            self._conn.commit()\n+        return self.get_change_webhook(watch_key) or {}\n+\n+    def get_change_webhook(self, watch_key: str) -> dict | None:\n+        with self._lock:\n+            row = self._conn.execute(\n+                \"SELECT webhook_url, secret, enabled FROM \"\n+                \"recheck_webhooks WHERE watch_key = ?\",\n+                (watch_key,),\n+            ).fetchone()\n+        if row is None:\n+            return None\n+        return {\"webhook_url\": row[0], \"secret\": row[1], \"enabled\": bool(row[2])}\n+\n+    def queue_change_delivery(\n+        self, event_id: str, watch_key: str, seq: int | None, url: str, payload: dict\n+    ) -> int:\n+        now = time.time()\n+        with self._lock:\n+            cur = self._conn.execute(\n+                \"INSERT INTO recheck_webhook_deliveries (event_id, \"\n+                \"watch_key, seq, url, status, created_epoch, \"\n+                \"updated_epoch, payload_json) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, \"\n+                \"'pending', ?, ?, ?)\",\n+                (\n+                    event_id,\n+                    watch_key,\n+                    seq,\n+                    url,\n+                    now,\n+                    now,\n+                    json.dumps(payload, sort_keys=True),\n+                ),\n+            )\n+            self._conn.commit()\n+            return int(cur.lastrowid)\n+\n+    def get_change_delivery(self, delivery_id: int) -> dict | None:\n+        with self._lock:\n+            row = self._conn.execute(\n+                \"SELECT id, event_id, watch_key, seq, url, status, \"\n+                \"attempts, last_http_status, last_error, payload_json \"\n+                \"FROM recheck_webhook_deliveries WHERE id = ?\",\n+                (int(delivery_id),),\n+            ).fetchone()\n+        if row is None:\n+            return None\n+        return {\n+            \"id\": row[0],\n+            \"event_id\": row[1],\n+            \"watch_key\": row[2],\n+            \"seq\": row[3],\n+            \"url\": row[4],\n+            \"status\": row[5],\n+            \"attempts\": row[6],\n+            \"last_http_status\": row[7],\n+            \"last_error\": row[8],\n+            \"payload\": json.loads(row[9]),\n+        }\n+\n+    def record_change_attempt(\n+        self,\n+        delivery_id: int,\n+        http_status: int | None,\n+        error: str | None,\n+    ) -> int:\n+        now = time.time()\n+        with self._lock:\n+            row = self._conn.execute(\n+                \"SELECT attempts FROM recheck_webhook_deliveries \"\n+                \"WHERE id = ?\",\n+                (int(delivery_id),),\n+            ).fetchone()\n+            attempt_no = int(row[0]) + 1 if row else 1\n+            self._conn.execute(\n+                \"INSERT INTO recheck_webhook_attempts (delivery_id, \"\n+                \"attempt_no, epoch, http_status, error) VALUES \"\n+                \"(?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n+                (int(delivery_id), attempt_no, now, http_status, error),\n+            )\n+            self._conn.execute(\n+                \"UPDATE recheck_webhook_deliveries SET attempts = ?, \"\n+                \"last_http_status = ?, last_error = ?, \"\n+                \"updated_epoch = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n+                (attempt_no, http_status, error, now, int(delivery_id)),\n+            )\n+            self._conn.commit()\n+        return attempt_no\n+\n+    def finish_change_delivery(self, delivery_id: int, status: str) -> None:\n+        with self._lock:\n+            self._conn.execute(\n+                \"UPDATE recheck_webhook_deliveries SET status = ?, \"\n+                \"updated_epoch = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n+                (status, time.time(), int(delivery_id)),\n+            )\n+            self._conn.commit()\n+\n+    def list_change_deliveries(\n+        self, watch_key: str | None = None, limit: int = 50\n+    ) -> list[dict]:\n+        clause = \"WHERE watch_key = ?\" if watch_key else \"\"\n+        params: tuple = (watch_key,) if watch_key else ()\n+        with self._lock:\n+            rows = self._conn.execute(\n+                \"SELECT id FROM recheck_webhook_deliveries \"\n+                f\"{clause} ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT ?\",\n+                (*params, max(1, min(int(limit), 500))),\n+            ).fetchall()\n+        return [\n+            d\n+            for d in (self.get_change_delivery(r[0]) for r in rows)\n+            if d is not None\n+        ]\n+\n     # --- watch packs ---------------------------------------------------\n     # Every pack mutation runs under the same lock as the watch state\n     # and commits before returning, so a spend is atomic in-process:\n@@ -2421,6 +2993,114 @@ def _diff(before: dict, after: dict) -> list[dict]:\n     return changes\n \n \n+# Structured field-level changes (additive to the legacy changes[]):\n+# {path, op, before, after, severity, category} with the same op /\n+# category vocabulary as RouteVerdict's diff. Derived from the\n+# fingerprint components the store actually keeps. For schema_hash\n+# the entry carries the hash before/after — the fingerprint stores\n+# the schema's hash, not the schema itself, so field-level detail\n+# INSIDE the target's schema is not available from Recheck (that is\n+# RouteVerdict's contract map's job, and the timeline joins them).\n+_FINGERPRINT_FIELD_CHANGES = {\n+    # fingerprint field -> (category, severity)\n+    \"amount\": (\"payment\", \"medium\"),\n+    \"payTo\": (\"payment\", \"high\"),\n+    \"network\": (\"payment\", \"medium\"),\n+    \"asset\": (\"payment\", \"medium\"),\n+    \"schema_hash\": (\"schema\", \"medium\"),\n+    \"description_hash\": (\"schema\", \"low\"),\n+    \"body_sha256\": (\"schema\", \"medium\"),\n+    \"status_code\": (\"listing\", \"high\"),\n+    \"kind\": (\"schema\", \"medium\"),\n+}\n+\n+\n+def fingerprint_field_changes(before: dict, after: dict) -> list[dict]:\n+    out: list[dict] = []\n+    for field in sorted(set(before) | set(after)):\n+        b, a = before.get(field), after.get(field)\n+        if b == a:\n+            continue\n+        category, severity = _FINGERPRINT_FIELD_CHANGES.get(\n+            field, (\"schema\", \"low\")\n+        )\n+        out.append(\n+            {\n+                \"path\": field,\n+                \"op\": \"value_changed\",\n+                \"before\": b,\n+                \"after\": a,\n+                \"severity\": severity,\n+                \"category\": category,\n+            }\n+        )\n+    return out\n+\n+\n+_HEX64 = frozenset(\"0123456789abcdef\")\n+\n+\n+def validate_imported_snapshot(\n+    kind: str, fingerprint: dict, schema: dict | None = None\n+) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Validate a snapshot offered for baseline import by\n+    RECOMPUTING what can be recomputed from its own fields. Raises\n+    ValueError with the reason; a forged snapshot (e.g. a schema\n+    that does not hash to the claimed schema_hash) never reaches\n+    the store. For an x402 snapshot carrying a schema_hash, the raw\n+    schema must be supplied and must hash to it — that is the\n+    fingerprint component an importer can actually prove. A web\n+    snapshot's body hash cannot be recomputed without the body, so\n+    web imports are validated structurally only (documented limit).\n+    \"\"\"\n+    if kind not in (\"x402\", \"web\"):\n+        raise ValueError(f\"kind must be 'x402' or 'web', got {kind!r}\")\n+    if not isinstance(fingerprint, dict):\n+        raise ValueError(\"fingerprint must be an object\")\n+    status = fingerprint.get(\"status_code\")\n+    if not isinstance(status, int):\n+        raise ValueError(\"fingerprint.status_code must be an integer\")\n+    if kind == \"x402\":\n+        for field in (\n+            \"amount\",\n+            \"asset\",\n+            \"network\",\n+            \"payTo\",\n+            \"description_hash\",\n+            \"schema_hash\",\n+        ):\n+            if field not in fingerprint:\n+                raise ValueError(f\"fingerprint is missing {field!r}\")\n+        for field in (\"description_hash\", \"schema_hash\"):\n+            value = fingerprint.get(field)\n+            if value is not None and not (\n+                isinstance(value, str)\n+                and len(value) == 64\n+                and all(c in _HEX64 for c in value.lower())\n+            ):\n+                raise ValueError(f\"fingerprint.{field} must be a sha256 hex digest or null\")\n+        if fingerprint.get(\"schema_hash\") is not None:\n+            if schema is None:\n+                raise ValueError(\n+                    \"this snapshot claims a schema_hash, so the raw \"\n+                    \"schema must be supplied to recompute it\"\n+                )\n+            recomputed = _hash_text(json.dumps(schema, sort_keys=True))\n+            if recomputed != fingerprint[\"schema_hash\"]:\n+                raise ValueError(\n+                    \"supplied schema does not hash to the snapshot's \"\n+                    \"schema_hash — import refused\"\n+                )\n+    else:\n+        body_hash = fingerprint.get(\"body_sha256\")\n+        if not (\n+            isinstance(body_hash, str)\n+            and len(body_hash) == 64\n+            and all(c in _HEX64 for c in body_hash.lower())\n+        ):\n+            raise ValueError(\"fingerprint.body_sha256 must be a sha256 hex digest\")\n+\n+\n async def recheck(\n     client: httpx.AsyncClient,\n     store: WatchStore,\n@@ -2436,7 +3116,10 @@ async def recheck(\n     key = f\"{wid}\\n{url}\"\n     kind, fingerprint = await _probe_fingerprint(client, url)\n     checked_at = _now_iso()\n-    prior = store.get(key)\n+    # A pinned baseline governs the diff while a pin exists; the\n+    # latest state still records every check, and unpinning returns\n+    # the watch to diffing against its latest state.\n+    prior = store.pinned_baseline(key) or store.get(key)\n     if prior is None:\n         store.save(key, kind, fingerprint, checked_at)\n         result = {\n@@ -2445,6 +3128,7 @@ async def recheck(\n             \"kind\": kind,\n             \"status\": \"BASELINE\",\n             \"changes\": [],\n+            \"field_changes\": [],\n             \"current\": fingerprint,\n             \"checked_at\": checked_at,\n             \"summary\": (\n@@ -2459,6 +3143,19 @@ async def recheck(\n         changes.insert(\n             0, {\"field\": \"kind\", \"before\": prior[\"kind\"], \"after\": kind}\n         )\n+    field_changes = fingerprint_field_changes(prior[\"fingerprint\"], fingerprint)\n+    if prior[\"kind\"] != kind:\n+        field_changes.insert(\n+            0,\n+            {\n+                \"path\": \"kind\",\n+                \"op\": \"value_changed\",\n+                \"before\": prior[\"kind\"],\n+                \"after\": kind,\n+                \"severity\": \"medium\",\n+                \"category\": \"schema\",\n+            },\n+        )\n     store.save(key, kind, fingerprint, checked_at)\n     if changes:\n         fields = \", \".join(c[\"field\"] for c in changes)\n@@ -2468,6 +3165,7 @@ async def recheck(\n             \"kind\": kind,\n             \"status\": \"CHANGED\",\n             \"changes\": changes,\n+            \"field_changes\": field_changes,\n             \"current\": fingerprint,\n             \"checked_at\": checked_at,\n             \"summary\": f\"Changed since the previous check: {fields}.\",\n@@ -2479,11 +3177,14 @@ async def recheck(\n             \"kind\": kind,\n             \"status\": \"UNCHANGED\",\n             \"changes\": [],\n+            \"field_changes\": field_changes,\n             \"current\": fingerprint,\n             \"checked_at\": checked_at,\n             \"summary\": \"No material change since the previous check.\",\n         }\n-    store.record_check(result)\n+    envelope = store.record_check(result)\n+    if result[\"status\"] == \"CHANGED\":\n+        _fire_change_webhook(client, store, envelope)\n     return result\n \n \n@@ -2513,3 +3214,149 @@ async def recheck_with_pack(\n     result[\"pack_credits_remaining\"] = reserved[\"credits_remaining\"]\n     result[\"pack_expires_at\"] = reserved[\"expires_at\"]\n     return result\n+\n+\n+# --- change webhooks ------------------------------------------------------\n+# A watch may carry one webhook (config is fleet-internal-secret\n+# gated at the HTTP layer). When a check for that watch answers\n+# CHANGED — never BASELINE or UNCHANGED — the recorded history\n+# envelope is delivered as a signed event: HMAC-SHA256 over the\n+# exact raw body bytes, keyed with the watch's secret, carried in\n+# X-Recheck-Signature beside X-Recheck-Event-Id. Delivery reuses\n+# the fleet's SSRF discipline (public addresses only, re-checked\n+# at send time), retries on a bounded backoff, records EVERY\n+# attempt, and lands in dead_letter after the final failure, where\n+# the authenticated deliveries read can see it.\n+\n+\n+def _change_webhook_backoffs() -> list[float]:\n+    raw = os.environ.get(\"STALLROW_RECHECK_WEBHOOK_BACKOFF_S\", \"1,4\")\n+    try:\n+        waits = [max(0.0, float(p)) for p in raw.split(\",\") if p.strip()]\n+    except ValueError:\n+        waits = [1.0, 4.0]\n+    return waits or [0.0]\n+\n+\n+def change_event_payload(envelope: dict) -> dict:\n+    record = envelope[\"record\"]\n+    return {\n+        \"event_id\": f\"evt_{envelope['record_id'][4:]}\",\n+        \"event\": \"recheck.changed\",\n+        \"seq\": envelope[\"seq\"],\n+        \"record_id\": envelope[\"record_id\"],\n+        \"record_hash\": envelope[\"record_hash\"],\n+        \"watch_id\": record[\"watch_id\"],\n+        \"url\": record[\"url\"],\n+        \"checked_at\": record[\"checked_at\"],\n+        \"field_changes\": record.get(\"field_changes\", []),\n+        \"record\": record,\n+    }\n+\n+\n+def queue_change_event(store: WatchStore, envelope: dict) -> int | None:\n+    \"\"\"Queue a CHANGED delivery if this watch has an enabled\n+    webhook. Returns the delivery id, or None (no config / disabled\n+    / not a change) — in which case nothing is recorded, because\n+    nothing was owed.\"\"\"\n+    record = envelope[\"record\"]\n+    if record.get(\"status\") != \"CHANGED\":\n+        return None\n+    key = f\"{record['watch_id']}\\n{record['url']}\"\n+    cfg = store.get_change_webhook(key)\n+    if cfg is None or not cfg[\"enabled\"]:\n+        return None\n+    payload = change_event_payload(envelope)\n+    return store.queue_change_delivery(\n+        payload[\"event_id\"], key, envelope[\"seq\"], record[\"url\"], payload\n+    )\n+\n+\n+async def deliver_change_event(\n+    client: httpx.AsyncClient, store: WatchStore, delivery_id: int\n+) -> dict:\n+    \"\"\"Attempt one queued delivery under the bounded retry\n+    discipline, recording every attempt on the delivery row. A\n+    target the SSRF guard refuses is dead on the first attempt —\n+    retrying a deterministic refusal buys nothing.\"\"\"\n+    delivery = store.get_change_delivery(delivery_id)\n+    if delivery is None:\n+        return {\"delivery_id\": delivery_id, \"status\": \"missing\"}\n+    cfg = store.get_change_webhook(delivery[\"watch_key\"])\n+    if cfg is None:\n+        store.record_change_attempt(\n+            delivery_id, None, \"webhook configuration removed before delivery\"\n+        )\n+        store.finish_change_delivery(delivery_id, \"dead_letter\")\n+        return {\"delivery_id\": delivery_id, \"status\": \"dead_letter\"}\n+    payload = delivery[\"payload\"]\n+    body = json.dumps(payload, sort_keys=True).encode(\"utf-8\")\n+    signature = hmac.new(\n+        cfg[\"secret\"].encode(\"utf-8\"), body, hashlib.sha256\n+    ).hexdigest()\n+    headers = {\n+        \"content-type\": \"application/json\",\n+        \"x-recheck-event-id\": payload[\"event_id\"],\n+        \"x-recheck-signature\": f\"sha256={signature}\",\n+    }\n+    url = cfg[\"webhook_url\"]\n+    try:\n+        await asyncio.to_thread(fetch_svc.ssrf_check, url)\n+    except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 - refusal is a recorded outcome\n+        store.record_change_attempt(\n+            delivery_id, None, f\"target refused by the SSRF guard: {exc}\"\n+        )\n+        store.finish_change_delivery(delivery_id, \"dead_letter\")\n+        return {\"delivery_id\": delivery_id, \"status\": \"dead_letter\"}\n+    waits = _change_webhook_backoffs()\n+    for attempt in range(len(waits) + 1):\n+        try:\n+            resp = await client.post(\n+                url,\n+                content=body,\n+                headers=headers,\n+                timeout=10.0,\n+                follow_redirects=False,\n+            )\n+            ok = 200 <= resp.status_code < 300\n+            store.record_change_attempt(\n+                delivery_id,\n+                resp.status_code,\n+                None if ok else f\"HTTP {resp.status_code}\",\n+            )\n+            if ok:\n+                store.finish_change_delivery(delivery_id, \"delivered\")\n+                return {\"delivery_id\": delivery_id, \"status\": \"delivered\"}\n+        except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 - recorded, then retried\n+            store.record_change_attempt(\n+                delivery_id, None, f\"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\"\n+            )\n+        if attempt < len(waits):\n+            await asyncio.sleep(waits[attempt])\n+    store.finish_change_delivery(delivery_id, \"dead_letter\")\n+    return {\"delivery_id\": delivery_id, \"status\": \"dead_letter\"}\n+\n+\n+def _fire_change_webhook(\n+    client: httpx.AsyncClient, store: WatchStore, envelope: dict\n+) -> None:\n+    \"\"\"Queue + schedule delivery from inside recheck(). Delivery\n+    health never fails the check that produced the event: queueing\n+    is synchronous (so the delivery row exists before the caller\n+    returns), sending is a background task on the caller's client.\"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        delivery_id = queue_change_event(store, envelope)\n+    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 - the check already answered\n+        log.exception(\"change webhook queueing failed\")\n+        return\n+    if delivery_id is None:\n+        return\n+    try:\n+        asyncio.get_running_loop().create_task(\n+            deliver_change_event(client, store, delivery_id)\n+        )\n+    except RuntimeError:  # no running loop — row stays pending, readable\n+        log.warning(\n+            \"change webhook delivery %s queued without a running loop\",\n+            delivery_id,\n+        )"},{"sha":"d92dfa1f9b6a2936e7baba62b143cf8cd4b4688f","filename":"app/services/timeline.py","status":"added","additions":119,"deletions":0,"changes":119,"blob_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB/stall-row/blob/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff/app%2Fservices%2Ftimeline.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB/stall-row/raw/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff/app%2Fservices%2Ftimeline.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuincyGB/stall-row/contents/app%2Fservices%2Ftimeline.py?ref=d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,119 @@\n+\"\"\"The unified per-resource timeline (GET /v1/resource/timeline).\n+\n+One URL-keyed read joining the three places the fleet already\n+records the truth about an x402 resource:\n+\n+  * Recheck events — StallRow's own feed history (full recorded\n+    response objects, with their feed seq / record_id).\n+  * RouteVerdict check events — read from RouteVerdict's own free\n+    GET /v1/history, because its check store lives inside that\n+    service; StallRow aggregates over HTTP and NEVER reaches into\n+    the sibling's database or invents its rows.\n+  * Catalogue state — StallRow's own CDP index snapshot store\n+    (services/indexfeed.py): what the latest catalogue snapshot\n+    holds for this resource, if anything.\n+\n+Every section names its source and its state (\"ok\" / \"no_records\" /\n+\"not_listed\" / \"unavailable\"). A source that fails is reported\n+unavailable — the timeline degrades honestly instead of filling\n+the gap. Events merge into one list ordered by checked_at.\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+from __future__ import annotations\n+\n+import httpx\n+\n+from . import indexfeed as indexfeed_svc\n+from . import orchestrate as orchestrate_svc\n+from . import recheck as recheck_svc\n+\n+_RV_TIMEOUT_S = 6.0\n+\n+\n+def _catalogue_block(index_store, url: str) -> tuple[dict | None, str]:\n+    \"\"\"(block, source_state) from the newest index snapshot.\"\"\"\n+    try:\n+        snapshots = index_store.snapshots()\n+    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 - a broken store is 'unavailable'\n+        return None, \"unavailable\"\n+    if not snapshots:\n+        return None, \"unavailable\"\n+    newest = snapshots[-1]\n+    try:\n+        entry = index_store.entries(newest[\"id\"]).get(url)\n+    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001\n+        return None, \"unavailable\"\n+    if entry is None:\n+        return None, \"not_listed\"\n+    return {\n+        \"source\": \"cdp_index_snapshot\",\n+        \"snapshot_id\": newest[\"id\"],\n+        \"captured_at\": newest[\"captured_at\"],\n+        \"entry\": entry,\n+    }, \"ok\"\n+\n+\n+async def build_timeline(\n+    client: httpx.AsyncClient,\n+    store: recheck_svc.WatchStore,\n+    index_store: indexfeed_svc.IndexStore,\n+    url: str,\n+) -> dict:\n+    url = url.strip()\n+    events: list[dict] = []\n+    sources: dict[str, str] = {}\n+\n+    rows = store.feed_rows(url=url, limit=1000, ascending=True)\n+    for env in rows:\n+        record = env[\"record\"]\n+        events.append(\n+            {\n+                \"source\": \"recheck\",\n+                \"seq\": env[\"seq\"],\n+                \"record_id\": env[\"record_id\"],\n+                \"checked_at\": record.get(\"checked_at\"),\n+                \"kind\": record.get(\"kind\"),\n+                \"status\": record.get(\"status\"),\n+                \"summary\": record.get(\"summary\"),\n+                \"changes\": record.get(\"changes\", []),\n+                \"field_changes\": record.get(\"field_changes\", []),\n+                \"current\": record.get(\"current\"),\n+            }\n+        )\n+    sources[\"recheck\"] = \"ok\" if rows else \"no_records\"\n+\n+    rv_base = orchestrate_svc._base(\"route_verdict\")\n+    try:\n+        resp = await client.get(\n+            f\"{rv_base}/v1/history\",\n+            params={\"resource_url\": url},\n+            timeout=_RV_TIMEOUT_S,\n+        )\n+        resp.raise_for_status()\n+        checks = resp.json().get(\"checks\") or []\n+        for check in checks:\n+            events.append(\n+                {\n+                    \"source\": \"route_verdict\",\n+                    \"checked_at\": check.get(\"checked_at\"),\n+                    \"verdict\": check.get(\"verdict\"),\n+                    \"score\": check.get(\"score\"),\n+                    \"diff\": check.get(\"diff\"),\n+                    \"terms\": check.get(\"terms\"),\n+                    \"catalog\": check.get(\"catalog\"),\n+                }\n+            )\n+        sources[\"route_verdict\"] = \"ok\" if checks else \"no_records\"\n+    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 - degraded, never fabricated\n+        sources[\"route_verdict\"] = \"unavailable\"\n+\n+    catalogue, catalogue_state = _catalogue_block(index_store, url)\n+    sources[\"catalogue_index\"] = catalogue_state\n+\n+    events.sort(key=lambda e: e.get(\"checked_at\") or \"\")\n+    return {\n+        \"url\": url,\n+        \"sources\": sources,\n+        \"catalogue\": catalogue,\n+        \"events\": events,\n+    }"},{"sha":"ac57155538c22dae3b9f414a2d2e63ccbd44e5fd","filename":"tests/test_recheck_v2.py","status":"added","additions":583,"deletions":0,"changes":583,"blob_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB/stall-row/blob/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff/tests%2Ftest_recheck_v2.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/QuincyGB/stall-row/raw/d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff/tests%2Ftest_recheck_v2.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/QuincyGB/stall-row/contents/tests%2Ftest_recheck_v2.py?ref=d71698264878f8daccec703b1d1f6d205aad47ff","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,583 @@\n+\"\"\"Feed v2 + baselines + field-level diffs + change webhooks +\n+the unified timeline (the 2026-10-29 aicom improvements 1–5).\n+\n+Fully offline: MockTransport plays targets and webhook receivers;\n+IP-literal URLs keep the SSRF guard's DNS lookup local.\n+\"\"\"\n+\n+import asyncio\n+import base64\n+import hashlib\n+import hmac\n+import json\n+import sqlite3\n+\n+import httpx\n+import pytest\n+from fastapi.testclient import TestClient\n+\n+import app.main as main\n+from app.services import indexfeed, recheck, timeline\n+\n+OWNER = \"0x097f9685D1e0752bF8B02d61E5Ce9be7eA0FBA7F\"\n+OTHER = \"0x2222222222222222222222222222222222222222\"\n+USDC = \"0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913\"\n+X402_URL = \"https://93.184.216.34/v1/verdict\"\n+HOOK_URL = \"https://93.184.216.34/hook\"\n+SECRET = \"fleet-test-secret\"\n+\n+\n+@pytest.fixture(autouse=True)\n+def _no_backoff(monkeypatch):\n+    monkeypatch.setattr(recheck, \"_BACKOFF_S\", (0, 0))\n+    monkeypatch.setenv(\"STALLROW_RECHECK_WEBHOOK_BACKOFF_S\", \"0,0\")\n+\n+\n+@pytest.fixture()\n+def store(tmp_path):\n+    return recheck.WatchStore(str(tmp_path / \"watches.db\"))\n+\n+\n+@pytest.fixture()\n+def http(store, monkeypatch):\n+    monkeypatch.setattr(main, \"_recheck_store\", store)\n+    return TestClient(main.app, raise_server_exceptions=False)\n+\n+\n+def _client(handler) -> httpx.AsyncClient:\n+    return httpx.AsyncClient(transport=httpx.MockTransport(handler))\n+\n+\n+def _challenge(amount=\"20000\", pay_to=OWNER, schema_type=\"string\"):\n+    return {\n+        \"x402Version\": 2,\n+        \"error\": \"Payment required\",\n+        \"resource\": {\n+            \"url\": X402_URL,\n+            \"description\": \"A target service.\",\n+            \"mimeType\": \"application/json\",\n+        },\n+        \"accepts\": [\n+            {\n+                \"scheme\": \"exact\",\n+                \"network\": \"eip155:8453\",\n+                \"asset\": USDC,\n+                \"amount\": amount,\n+                \"payTo\": pay_to,\n+                \"maxTimeoutSeconds\": 300,\n+            }\n+        ],\n+        \"extensions\": {\n+            \"bazaar\": {\n+                \"info\": {\n+                    \"input\": {\"type\": \"http\", \"method\": \"POST\", \"bodyType\": \"json\", \"body\": {}},\n+                    \"output\": {\n+                        \"type\": \"json\",\n+                        \"schema\": {\n+                            \"type\": \"object\",\n+                            \"properties\": {\"verdict\": {\"type\": schema_type}},\n+                            \"required\": [\"verdict\"],\n+                        },\n+                    },\n+                }\n+            }\n+        },\n+    }\n+\n+\n+def _challenge_response(**kw) -> httpx.Response:\n+    challenge = _challenge(**kw)\n+    raw = base64.b64encode(json.dumps(challenge).encode()).decode()\n+    return httpx.Response(402, headers={\"payment-required\": raw}, json=challenge)\n+\n+\n+def _record(store, watch_id=\"w1\", url=X402_URL, amount=\"100\", n=0):\n+    return store.record_check(\n+        {\n+            \"watch_id\": watch_id,\n+            \"url\": url,\n+            \"kind\": \"x402\",\n+            \"status\": \"UNCHANGED\",\n+            \"changes\": [],\n+            \"field_changes\": [],\n+            \"current\": {\"amount\": amount, \"payTo\": OWNER},\n+            \"checked_at\": f\"2026-10-29T00:{n % 60:02d}:00Z\",\n+            \"summary\": \"synthetic\",\n+        }\n+    )\n+\n+\n+# --- item 2: seq + hash chain ---------------------------------------------------\n+\n+\n+def test_chain_is_continuous_and_verifies(store):\n+    envs = [_record(store, n=i) for i in range(3)]\n+    assert [e[\"seq\"] for e in envs] == [1, 2, 3]\n+    assert envs[0][\"prev_hash\"] == \"genesis\"\n+    assert envs[1][\"prev_hash\"] == envs[0][\"record_hash\"]\n+    assert envs[2][\"prev_hash\"] == envs[1][\"record_hash\"]\n+    assert all(e[\"record_id\"].startswith(\"rec_\") for e in envs)\n+    assert store.verify_chain() is True\n+    assert store.latest_seq() == 3\n+\n+\n+def test_backfill_is_deterministic_and_idempotent(tmp_path):\n+    path = str(tmp_path / \"watches.db\")\n+    store = recheck.WatchStore(path)\n+    _record(store, n=1)\n+    _record(store, n=2)\n+    before = [(e[\"seq\"], e[\"record_hash\"]) for e in store.feed_rows(ascending=True)]\n+    store.close()\n+    # Simulate a pre-v2 store: wipe the chain, keep the records.\n+    conn = sqlite3.connect(path)\n+    conn.execute(\"UPDATE recheck_history SET seq=NULL, record_id=NULL, schema_version=NULL, prev_hash=NULL, record_hash=NULL\")\n+    conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM feed_meta\")\n+    conn.commit()\n+    conn.close()\n+    reopened = recheck.WatchStore(path)\n+    after = [(e[\"seq\"], e[\"record_hash\"]) for e in reopened.feed_rows(ascending=True)]\n+    assert after == before\n+    assert reopened.verify_chain() is True\n+    reopened.close()\n+    again = recheck.WatchStore(path)\n+    assert [(e[\"seq\"], e[\"record_hash\"]) for e in again.feed_rows(ascending=True)] == before\n+\n+\n+def test_cursor_pagination_over_100_records_has_no_gaps(store):\n+    for i in range(150):\n+        _record(store, n=i)\n+    page1 = store.feed_rows(since_seq=0, limit=100)\n+    page2 = store.feed_rows(since_seq=page1[-1][\"seq\"], limit=100)\n+    seqs = [e[\"seq\"] for e in page1 + page2]\n+    assert seqs == list(range(1, 151))\n+    # filters\n+    assert store.feed_rows(watch_id=\"w1\", url=X402_URL, limit=1000)\n+    assert store.feed_rows(watch_id=\"nobody\") == []\n+    assert store.feed_rows(url=\"https://elsewhere.example/x\") == []\n+\n+\n+def test_feed_endpoint_legacy_shape_and_v2_cursor(http, store):\n+    for i in range(3):\n+        _record(store, n=i)\n+    legacy = http.get(\"/v1/recheck/feed\")\n+    assert legacy.status_code == 200\n+    assert legacy.headers[\"x-recheck-feed-latest-seq\"] == \"3\"\n+    lines = [json.loads(l) for l in legacy.text.splitlines()]\n+    assert all(\"seq\" not in l for l in lines)  # bare response objects\n+    assert [l[\"checked_at\"] for l in lines] == [\n+        \"2026-10-29T00:02:00Z\",\n+        \"2026-10-29T00:01:00Z\",\n+        \"2026-10-29T00:00:00Z\",\n+    ]\n+    v2 = http.get(\"/v1/recheck/feed\", params={\"since_seq\": 1})\n+    envs = [json.loads(l) for l in v2.text.splitlines()]\n+    assert [e[\"seq\"] for e in envs] == [2, 3]\n+    assert envs[0][\"record\"][\"checked_at\"] == \"2026-10-29T00:01:00Z\"\n+    assert v2.headers[\"x-recheck-feed-first-seq\"] == \"2\"\n+    assert v2.headers[\"x-recheck-feed-last-seq\"] == \"3\"\n+\n+\n+def test_history_endpoint_and_stateless_compare(http, store):\n+    _record(store, amount=\"100\", n=1)\n+    _record(store, amount=\"200\", n=2)\n+    body = http.get(\n+        \"/v1/recheck/history\", params={\"watch_id\": \"w1\", \"url\": X402_URL}\n+    ).json()\n+    assert body[\"count\"] == 2\n+    assert body[\"latest_seq\"] == 2\n+    compared = http.get(\n+        \"/v1/recheck/history\",\n+        params={\"watch_id\": \"w1\", \"url\": X402_URL, \"compare_seq\": 1},\n+    ).json()\n+    fc = compared[\"comparison\"][\"field_changes\"]\n+    assert fc == [\n+        {\n+            \"path\": \"amount\",\n+            \"op\": \"value_changed\",\n+            \"before\": \"100\",\n+            \"after\": \"200\",\n+            \"severity\": \"medium\",\n+            \"category\": \"payment\",\n+        }\n+    ]\n+    one = http.get(f\"/v1/recheck/history/{body['records'][0]['record_id']}\")\n+    assert one.status_code == 200\n+    assert one.json()[\"seq\"] == 1\n+    assert http.get(\"/v1/recheck/history/rec_nope\").status_code == 404\n+\n+\n+# --- item 4: field-level diffs through recheck() ---------------------------------\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio\n+async def test_recheck_field_changes_name_the_mutated_fields(store):\n+    state = {\"amount\": \"20000\", \"pay_to\": OWNER, \"schema_type\": \"string\"}\n+\n+    def handler(request):\n+        return _challenge_response(**state)\n+\n+    async with _client(handler) as client:\n+        first = await recheck.recheck(client, store, X402_URL)\n+        assert first[\"field_changes\"] == []\n+        state[\"amount\"] = \"25000\"\n+        state[\"pay_to\"] = OTHER\n+        state[\"schema_type\"] = \"number\"\n+        changed = await recheck.recheck(client, store, X402_URL)\n+    assert changed[\"status\"] == \"CHANGED\"\n+    by_path = {fc[\"path\"]: fc for fc in changed[\"field_changes\"]}\n+    assert by_path[\"amount\"][\"before\"] == \"20000\"\n+    assert by_path[\"amount\"][\"after\"] == \"25000\"\n+    assert by_path[\"amount\"][\"category\"] == \"payment\"\n+    assert by_path[\"payTo\"][\"severity\"] == \"high\"\n+    assert by_path[\"schema_hash\"][\"before\"] != by_path[\"schema_hash\"][\"after\"]\n+    assert by_path[\"schema_hash\"][\"category\"] == \"schema\"\n+    # legacy changes[] untouched in shape\n+    assert {c[\"field\"] for c in changed[\"changes\"]} == {\n+        \"amount\",\n+        \"payTo\",\n+        \"schema_hash\",\n+    }\n+\n+\n+# --- item 3: pins + imports --------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio\n+async def test_pin_governs_the_diff_until_unpinned(store):\n+    state = {\"amount\": \"20000\"}\n+\n+    def handler(request):\n+        return _challenge_response(amount=state[\"amount\"])\n+\n+    async with _client(handler) as client:\n+        await recheck.recheck(client, store, X402_URL)  # seq 1, baseline\n+        state[\"amount\"] = \"25000\"\n+        changed = await recheck.recheck(client, store, X402_URL)\n+        assert changed[\"status\"] == \"CHANGED\"\n+        key = f\"{recheck.default_watch_id(X402_URL)}\\n{X402_URL}\"\n+        assert store.pin_baseline(key, 1, source=\"test\") is not None\n+        # Still the mutated state — against LATEST state this would be\n+        # UNCHANGED; against the pin it must report CHANGED again.\n+        again = await recheck.recheck(client, store, X402_URL)\n+        assert again[\"status\"] == \"CHANGED\"\n+        assert store.unpin_baseline(key) is True\n+        settled = await recheck.recheck(client, store, X402_URL)\n+        assert settled[\"status\"] == \"UNCHANGED\"\n+\n+\n+def _importable(schema=None):\n+    schema = schema or {\n+        \"type\": \"object\",\n+        \"properties\": {\"verdict\": {\"type\": \"string\"}},\n+        \"required\": [\"verdict\"],\n+    }\n+    fingerprint = {\n+        \"status_code\": 402,\n+        \"amount\": \"20000\",\n+        \"asset\": USDC,\n+        \"network\": \"eip155:8453\",\n+        \"payTo\": OWNER,\n+        \"description_hash\": None,\n+        \"schema_hash\": recheck._hash_text(json.dumps(schema, sort_keys=True)),\n+    }\n+    return fingerprint, schema\n+\n+\n+def test_import_validates_by_recomputation(store):\n+    fingerprint, schema = _importable()\n+    recheck.validate_imported_snapshot(\"x402\", fingerprint, schema)\n+    key = f\"imported-watch\\n{X402_URL}\"\n+    env = store.import_baseline(\n+        key, \"x402\", fingerprint, \"2026-10-20T00:00:00Z\", source=\"test-import\"\n+    )\n+    assert env[\"record\"][\"imported\"] is True\n+    assert env[\"record\"][\"provenance\"][\"source\"] == \"test-import\"\n+    assert store.get(key)[\"fingerprint\"] == fingerprint\n+\n+\n+def test_import_forged_schema_is_refused_loudly(store):\n+    fingerprint, schema = _importable()\n+    forged = {**schema, \"properties\": {\"verdict\": {\"type\": \"number\"}}}\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"does not hash\"):\n+        recheck.validate_imported_snapshot(\"x402\", fingerprint, forged)\n+    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"must be supplied\"):\n+        recheck.validate_imported_snapshot(\"x402\", fingerprint, None)\n+    assert store.check_history_count() == 0\n+\n+\n+def test_internal_mutations_are_secret_gated(http, store, monkeypatch):\n+    monkeypatch.delenv(\"FLEET_INTERNAL_SECRET\", raising=False)\n+    r = http.post(\n+        \"/v1/internal/recheck/baseline/pin\",\n+        json={\"url\": X402_URL, \"seq\": 1},\n+    )\n+    assert r.status_code == 404  # no secret configured, no endpoint\n+    monkeypatch.setenv(\"FLEET_INTERNAL_SECRET\", SECRET)\n+    r = http.post(\n+        \"/v1/internal/recheck/baseline/pin\",\n+        json={\"url\": X402_URL, \"seq\": 1},\n+        headers={\"x-fleet-internal-secret\": \"wrong\"},\n+    )\n+    assert r.status_code == 403\n+    _record(store, watch_id=recheck.default_watch_id(X402_URL), n=1)\n+    r = http.post(\n+        \"/v1/internal/recheck/baseline/pin\",\n+        json={\"url\": X402_URL, \"seq\": 1},\n+        headers={\"x-fleet-internal-secret\": SECRET},\n+    )\n+    assert r.status_code == 200\n+    assert r.json()[\"pin\"][\"seq\"] == 1\n+    fingerprint, schema = _importable()\n+    r = http.post(\n+        \"/v1/internal/recheck/baseline/import\",\n+        json={\n+            \"url\": X402_URL,\n+            \"kind\": \"x402\",\n+            \"current\": fingerprint,\n+            \"checked_at\": \"2026-10-20T00:00:00Z\",\n+            \"source\": \"test\",\n+            \"schema\": {**schema, \"properties\": {\"verdict\": {\"type\": \"number\"}}},\n+        },\n+        headers={\"x-fleet-internal-secret\": SECRET},\n+    )\n+    assert r.status_code == 422  # forged: schema doesn't hash to the claim\n+    assert store.check_history_count() == 1  # nothing was stored\n+\n+\n+# --- item 5: change webhooks --------------------------------------------------------\n+\n+\n+def _watch_key(watch_id=\"hookwatch\"):\n+    return f\"{watch_id}\\n{X402_URL}\"\n+\n+\n+def _changed_envelope(store, watch_id=\"hookwatch\"):\n+    return store.record_check(\n+        {\n+            \"watch_id\": watch_id,\n+            \"url\": X402_URL,\n+            \"kind\": \"x402\",\n+            \"status\": \"CHANGED\",\n+            \"changes\": [{\"field\": \"amount\", \"before\": \"1\", \"after\": \"2\"}],\n+            \"field_changes\": [\n+                {\n+                    \"path\": \"amount\",\n+                    \"op\": \"value_changed\",\n+                    \"before\": \"1\",\n+                    \"after\": \"2\",\n+                    \"severity\": \"medium\",\n+                    \"category\": \"payment\",\n+                }\n+            ],\n+            \"current\": {\"amount\": \"2\"},\n+            \"checked_at\": \"2026-10-29T01:00:00Z\",\n+            \"summary\": \"Changed since the previous check: amount.\",\n+        }\n+    )\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio\n+async def test_webhook_delivery_is_signed_and_recorded(store):\n+    store.set_change_webhook(_watch_key(), HOOK_URL, \"whsec_test\")\n+    envelope = _changed_envelope(store)\n+    delivery_id = recheck.queue_change_event(store, envelope)\n+    assert delivery_id is not None\n+    seen = {}\n+\n+    def handler(request):\n+        seen[\"body\"] = request.content\n+        seen[\"sig\"] = request.headers.get(\"x-recheck-signature\")\n+        seen[\"event\"] = request.headers.get(\"x-recheck-event-id\")\n+        return httpx.Response(200, text=\"ok\")\n+\n+    async with _client(handler) as client:\n+        out = await recheck.deliver_change_event(client, store, delivery_id)\n+    assert out[\"status\"] == \"delivered\"\n+    expected = hmac.new(b\"whsec_test\", seen[\"body\"], hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n+    assert seen[\"sig\"] == f\"sha256={expected}\"\n+    payload = json.loads(seen[\"body\"])\n+    assert payload[\"event\"] == \"recheck.changed\"\n+    assert payload[\"field_changes\"][0][\"path\"] == \"amount\"\n+    assert seen[\"event\"] == payload[\"event_id\"]\n+    row = store.get_change_delivery(delivery_id)\n+    assert row[\"status\"] == \"delivered\"\n+    assert row[\"attempts\"] == 1\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio\n+async def test_webhook_dead_letter_after_bounded_retries(store):\n+    store.set_change_webhook(_watch_key(), HOOK_URL, \"whsec_test\")\n+    delivery_id = recheck.queue_change_event(store, _changed_envelope(store))\n+\n+    def handler(request):\n+        return httpx.Response(500, text=\"no\")\n+\n+    async with _client(handler) as client:\n+        out = await recheck.deliver_change_event(client, store, delivery_id)\n+    assert out[\"status\"] == \"dead_letter\"\n+    row = store.get_change_delivery(delivery_id)\n+    assert row[\"status\"] == \"dead_letter\"\n+    assert row[\"attempts\"] == 3  # backoff list \"0,0\" -> 3 attempts\n+    assert row[\"last_http_status\"] == 500\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio\n+async def test_webhook_ssrf_target_dies_without_any_http_attempt(store):\n+    store.set_change_webhook(\n+        _watch_key(), \"https://169.254.169.254/hook\", \"whsec_test\"\n+    )\n+    delivery_id = recheck.queue_change_event(store, _changed_envelope(store))\n+    calls = {\"n\": 0}\n+\n+    def handler(request):\n+        calls[\"n\"] += 1\n+        return httpx.Response(200)\n+\n+    async with _client(handler) as client:\n+        out = await recheck.deliver_change_event(client, store, delivery_id)\n+    assert out[\"status\"] == \"dead_letter\"\n+    assert calls[\"n\"] == 0\n+    row = store.get_change_delivery(delivery_id)\n+    assert row[\"attempts\"] == 1\n+    assert \"SSRF\" in (row[\"last_error\"] or \"\")\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio\n+async def test_recheck_fires_only_on_changed(store):\n+    store.set_change_webhook(\n+        f\"{recheck.default_watch_id(X402_URL)}\\n{X402_URL}\",\n+        HOOK_URL,\n+        \"whsec_test\",\n+    )\n+    state = {\"amount\": \"20000\"}\n+    hits = {\"n\": 0}\n+\n+    def handler(request):\n+        if str(request.url).endswith(\"/hook\"):\n+            hits[\"n\"] += 1\n+            return httpx.Response(200, text=\"ok\")\n+        return _challenge_response(amount=state[\"amount\"])\n+\n+    async with _client(handler) as client:\n+        await recheck.recheck(client, store, X402_URL)  # BASELINE\n+        await recheck.recheck(client, store, X402_URL)  # UNCHANGED\n+        assert store.list_change_deliveries() == []\n+        state[\"amount\"] = \"25000\"\n+        await recheck.recheck(client, store, X402_URL)  # CHANGED\n+        for _ in range(50):\n+            rows = store.list_change_deliveries()\n+            if rows and rows[0][\"status\"] == \"delivered\":\n+                break\n+            await asyncio.sleep(0.02)\n+    rows = store.list_change_deliveries()\n+    assert len(rows) == 1\n+    assert rows[0][\"status\"] == \"delivered\"\n+    assert hits[\"n\"] == 1\n+\n+\n+def test_webhook_config_endpoint_rejects_bad_targets(http, monkeypatch):\n+    monkeypatch.setenv(\"FLEET_INTERNAL_SECRET\", SECRET)\n+    headers = {\"x-fleet-internal-secret\": SECRET}\n+    r = http.post(\n+        \"/v1/internal/recheck/webhooks\",\n+        json={\"url\": X402_URL, \"webhook_url\": \"http://93.184.216.34/hook\", \"secret\": \"s\"},\n+        headers=headers,\n+    )\n+    assert r.status_code == 422  # not https\n+    r = http.post(\n+        \"/v1/internal/recheck/webhooks\",\n+        json={\"url\": X402_URL, \"webhook_url\": \"https://169.254.169.254/hook\", \"secret\": \"s\"},\n+        headers=headers,\n+    )\n+    assert r.status_code == 422  # SSRF-refused\n+    r = http.post(\n+        \"/v1/internal/recheck/webhooks\",\n+        json={\"url\": X402_URL, \"webhook_url\": HOOK_URL, \"secret\": \"s3cr3t\"},\n+        headers=headers,\n+    )\n+    assert r.status_code == 200\n+    assert \"s3cr3t\" not in r.text  # secret never echoed\n+\n+\n+# --- item 1: unified timeline ---------------------------------------------------\n+\n+\n+def _rv_history_handler(checks):\n+    def handler(request):\n+        if request.url.host == \"route-verdict-production.up.railway.app\":\n+            return httpx.Response(\n+                200, json={\"resource_url\": X402_URL, \"count\": len(checks), \"checks\": checks}\n+            )\n+        raise httpx.ConnectError(\"nope\", request=request)\n+\n+    return handler\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio\n+async def test_timeline_merges_all_three_sources(store, tmp_path):\n+    # Alex's watch, in the shape his Oct 29 records carry.\n+    store.record_check(\n+        {\n+            \"watch_id\": \"modelmarket-survey\",\n+            \"url\": \"https://modelmarket.dev/x402/histor-check\",\n+            \"kind\": \"x402\",\n+            \"status\": \"CHANGED\",\n+            \"changes\": [{\"field\": \"schema_hash\", \"before\": None, \"after\": \"7cbf\"}],\n+            \"field_changes\": [],\n+            \"current\": {\"amount\": \"1000\", \"schema_hash\": \"7cbf\"},\n+            \"checked_at\": \"2026-10-29T19:04:42Z\",\n+            \"summary\": \"Changed since the previous check: schema_hash.\",\n+        }\n+    )\n+    url = \"https://modelmarket.dev/x402/histor-check\"\n+    rv_checks = [\n+        {\n+            \"resource_url\": url,\n+            \"checked_at\": \"2026-10-29T19:04:00Z\",\n+            \"verdict\": \"TRUSTED\",\n+            \"score\": 95.0,\n+            \"diff\": {\"contract_stability\": \"unknown\"},\n+            \"terms\": {\"amount_units\": \"1000\"},\n+            \"catalog\": {},\n+        }\n+    ]\n+\n+    def handler(request):\n+        return httpx.Response(\n+            200, json={\"resource_url\": url, \"count\": 1, \"checks\": rv_checks}\n+        )\n+\n+    idx = indexfeed.IndexStore(str(tmp_path / \"index.db\"))\n+    idx.save_snapshot(\n+        [{\"resource\": url, \"serviceName\": \"aicom\", \"amount\": \"1000\"}],\n+        epoch=1760000000.0,\n+    )\n+    async with _client(handler) as client:\n+        out = await timeline.build_timeline(client, store, idx, url)\n+    assert out[\"sources\"] == {\n+        \"recheck\": \"ok\",\n+        \"route_verdict\": \"ok\",\n+        \"catalogue_index\": \"ok\",\n+    }\n+    assert out[\"catalogue\"][\"entry\"][\"serviceName\"] == \"aicom\"\n+    assert [e[\"source\"] for e in out[\"events\"]] == [\"route_verdict\", \"recheck\"]\n+    recheck_event = out[\"events\"][1]\n+    assert recheck_event[\"status\"] == \"CHANGED\"\n+    assert recheck_event[\"seq\"] == 1\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio\n+async def test_timeline_degrades_honestly(store, tmp_path):\n+    def handler(request):\n+        raise httpx.ConnectError(\"down\", request=request)\n+\n+    idx = indexfeed.IndexStore(str(tmp_path / \"index.db\"))\n+    async with _client(handler) as client:\n+        out = await timeline.build_timeline(\n+            client, store, idx, \"https://modelmarket.dev/x402/histor-check\"\n+        )\n+    assert out[\"sources\"][\"route_verdict\"] == \"unavailable\"\n+    assert out[\"sources\"][\"recheck\"] == \"no_records\"\n+    assert out[\"sources\"][\"catalogue_index\"] == \"unavailable\"\n+    assert out[\"events\"] == []\n+    assert out[\"catalogue\"] is None"}]}